  "text": "Have you ever felt anxious about your future, wondering if everything will be okay? You pray, you try to stay strong, but deep inside, your mind is filled with worry. So, how can you trust God when anxiety feels overwhelming? The Bible gives us a powerful answer. In Philippians chapter four, verses six and seven, we are encouraged to bring our worries to God through prayer and thanksgiving. Notice what this means. God is not asking you to pretend that your problems do not exist. He is inviting you to bring those problems to Him. When fear fills your mind, you can speak honestly to God about what you are feeling. Tell Him what worries you. Ask Him for wisdom, strength, and peace. And remember the words of Psalm fifty-six, verse three. When I am afraid, I will trust in You. This does not mean fear will disappear instantly. It means that even when you feel afraid, you can choose to turn toward God instead of facing your fear alone. Jesus also reminds us in Matthew chapter six that we should not be consumed by worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow has its own concerns, but today is the day you are living right now. So, take one step at a time. Pray when your thoughts feel heavy. Read God's Word when you need direction. And reach out to someone you trust when you need support. Faith is not about having every answer. It is about learning to trust God, even when you cannot see the whole picture. You may not know what tomorrow will bring, but you can seek God's guidance today. When anxiety rises, remember this. You do not have to carry every worry alone. Bring your fears to God, take the next step with faith, and give yourself grace along the way. If this message encouraged you, take a moment to reflect on this question. What is one worry you can bring to God today?",
